level1 lfo10;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>We&#8217;re now in feature =
freeze for 3.0 and working on bug fixing for final =
release<o:p></o:p></span></li><li class=3DMsoNormal =
style=3D'color:black;mso-list:l7 level1 =
lfo10;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>We have not built M3 yet as =
some work still remains for us to be feature complete and ready for QA. =
This puts us behind schedule but the plan is to complete the key =
features we&#8217;ve planned rather than adhere strictly to dates. We =
hope to make up time during M4 by having M3 at high quality and take =
advantage of our automation.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li class=3DMsoNormal =
style=3D'color:black;mso-list:l7 level1 =
lfo10;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>RP is away for the rest of the =
week which means M3 progress will be limited this week, Ross will queue =
patches.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li class=3DMsoNormal =
style=3D'color:black;mso-list:l7 level1 =
lfo10;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Key 3.0 changes have now =
merged:<o:p></o:p></span></li><ul style=3D'margin-top:0in' =
type=3Dcircle><li class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'color:black;mso-list:l7 =
level2 lfo10;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>5.2 =
linux-libc-kernel-headers<o:p></o:p></span></li><li class=3DMsoNormal =
style=3D'color:black;mso-list:l7 level2 =
lfo10;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>5.2 kernel recipes by default =
for all reference BSPs<o:p></o:p></span></li><li class=3DMsoNormal =
style=3D'color:black;mso-list:l7 level2 =
lfo10;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Removal of LSB and poky-lsb and =
replacement with alt config testing<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'color:black;mso-list:l7 level2 =
lfo10;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>systemd by default for =
poky-altcfg<o:p></o:p></span></li><li class=3DMsoNormal =
style=3D'color:black;mso-list:l7 level2 =
lfo10;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Patches have significantly =
reduced the dependency on python2<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'color:black;mso-list:l7 level2 =
lfo10;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Reproducible builds are now =
being tested for core-image-minimal<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'color:black;mso-list:l7 level2 =
lfo10;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Automated toolchain testsuite =
tests (binutils, gcc, glibc)<o:p></o:p></span></li></ul><li =
class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'color:black;mso-list:l7 level1 =
lfo10;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Key blocking issues for M3 that =
have been fixed:<o:p></o:p></span></li><ul style=3D'margin-top:0in' =
type=3Dcircle><li class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'color:black;mso-list:l7 =
level2 lfo10;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Systemtap issues with 5.2 were =
debugged and patches sent/merged upstream<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'color:black;mso-list:l7 level2 =
lfo10;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>5.2 dmesg on qemuarm64 =
fixed<o:p></o:p></span></li><li class=3DMsoNormal =
style=3D'color:black;mso-list:l7 level2 =
lfo10;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>qemumips hang when using =
highmem root caused and worked around (for =
now)<o:p></o:p></span></li><li class=3DMsoNormal =
style=3D'color:black;mso-list:l7 level2 =
lfo10;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>mdadm ptest timeout worked =
around<o:p></o:p></span></li><li class=3DMsoNormal =
style=3D'color:black;mso-list:l7 level2 =
lfo10;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>quilt and libevent ptest =
regressions from M2 resolved<o:p></o:p></span></li></ul><li =
class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'color:black;mso-list:l7 level1 =
lfo10;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Remaining issues blocking =
M3:<o:p></o:p></span></li><ul style=3D'margin-top:0in' type=3Dcircle><li =
class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'color:black;mso-list:l7 level2 =
lfo10;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>systemd boot failure on =
qemumips<o:p></o:p></span></li><li class=3DMsoNormal =
style=3D'color:black;mso-list:l7 level2 =
lfo10;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>strace ptest =
timeout<o:p></o:p></span></li><li class=3DMsoNormal =
style=3D'color:black;mso-list:l7 level2 =
lfo10;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Hash equivalence performance =
problems (RP has a simple idea to ~double =
speed)<o:p></o:p></span></li><li class=3DMsoNormal =
style=3D'color:black;mso-list:l7 level2 =
lfo10;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Hash equivalence =
bugs<o:p></o:p></span></li><li class=3DMsoNormal =
style=3D'color:black;mso-list:l7 level2 =
lfo10;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Toolchain testsuite relocation =
bugs (Nathan working on it)<o:p></o:p></span></li></ul><li =
class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'color:black;mso-list:l7 level1 =
lfo10;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Hash Equivalency =
status:<o:p></o:p></span></li><ul style=3D'margin-top:0in' =
type=3Dcircle><li class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'color:black;mso-list:l7 =
level2 lfo10;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Ideas about removing some =
dependency information from the hashes to allow faster bulk queries =
aren&#8217;t viable so the current codebase approach is =
correct<o:p></o:p></span></li><li class=3DMsoNormal =
style=3D'color:black;mso-list:l7 level2 =
lfo10;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>we need to rework the =
client/server communication to scale to the =
autobuilder<o:p></o:p></span></li><li class=3DMsoNormal =
style=3D'color:black;mso-list:l7 level2 =
lfo10;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>there are some bugs in the code =
the autobuilder continues to expose<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'color:black;mso-list:l7 level2 =
lfo10;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>we have cases where its not =
100% clear what the correct behaviour should =
be<o:p></o:p></span></li><li class=3DMsoNormal =
style=3D'color:black;mso-list:l7 level2 =
lfo10;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>test cases are proving to be =
problematic to write in a maintainable =
way<o:p></o:p></span></li></ul><li class=3DMsoNormal =
style=3D'color:black;mso-list:l7 level1 =
lfo10;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Documentation - Due to illness =
Scott is unavailable for the next month or two so doc patches will be =
handled by Richard or Ross in the short term. We&#8217;ll likely limit =
them to correctness issues and defer any substantial new text. If anyone =
has availability and skills to work on the manuals please talk to us. =
We&#8217;re aware there is a patch backlog.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'color:black;mso-list:l7 level1 =
